From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: clavin <clavin@electronjs.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:29:42 -0700
Subject: fix: gate webstorePrivate on a delegated availability check

The Chrome Web Store branch of the core webstorePrivate feature exposes
the API to web pages on that origin, but the browser-side implementation
requires an embedder-provided WebstorePrivateAPIDelegate that Electron
does not have. Require a delegated availability check on that branch, as
the testing branch already does. Electron never registers one, so the
feature fails closed in every context.

Electron previously did this by overriding the feature from its own
_api_features.json, which relied on later registrations replacing
earlier ones. Generated features are now immutable, so the override has
to be made in the core definition.

diff --git a/extensions/common/api/_api_features.json b/extensions/common/api/_api_features.json
index 48377da2780b58173cdd0da5aad816923119a709..9fbebc3cb45523f074b8c968a52052f230b368b6 100644
--- a/extensions/common/api/_api_features.json
+++ b/extensions/common/api/_api_features.json
@@ -968,6 +968,10 @@
   "webstorePrivate": [{
     "channel": "stable",
     "contexts": ["web_page"],
+    // Electron has no WebstorePrivateAPIDelegate and never registers a
+    // delegated availability check, so gating this branch like the testing
+    // one below makes the feature fail closed in every context.
+    "requires_delegated_availability_check": true,
     "matches": ["https://chromewebstore.google.com/*"]
   }, {
     // Used for webstore testing. See comment in
